From e19a874c8da2137aa5f748e8c7441573b662818a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 19:06:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] D9a: a statement fetched from Gmail gets the card's digits,
 as an upload does

SBI Card, Canara and HSBC lock their statements with the card number.
POST /import/pdf hands passwordCandidates the destination account's last
four; the Gmail statement path called it with none, so the same file that
opened when uploaded was counted "could not open" when it arrived by mail.
Verified first: a fictional SBI Card statement locked with DOB + card 4321
opened through /import/pdf and failed through /gmail/fetch.

The Gmail path now offers the last four of the one account at the sender's
bank it routes to and of that account's cards; when the route is unknown
(no account at that bank, or several) it offers every visible account's
and card's digits, so a statement that opens but has nowhere to go is
reported as unmatched rather than locked. Other members' private accounts
are not offered. Nothing is logged or stored: the digits are only tried.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
